From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zinee-u <suzinee.u@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: wifi: ameba: reject connect before station start

The vendor Wi-Fi initialization runs asynchronously. A management connect
request can therefore reach wifi_connect_zephyr() before the station adapter
has been created, which causes a fault in the vendor join path.

Use the vendor readiness query and return -EAGAIN while initialization is
incomplete. This leaves reconnects available after a normal disassociation,
which does not stop the station.

Signed-off-by: zinee-u <suzinee.u@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
--- a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
@@ -378,6 +378,11 @@ static int ameba_wifi_connect(const struct device *dev, struct net_if *iface,
 	uint8_t channel, psk_len;
 	uint8_t *psk;
 
+	if (!wifi_is_running(STA_WLAN_INDEX)) {
+		LOG_WRN("Wi-Fi station initialization is not complete");
+		return -EAGAIN;
+	}
+
 	net_eth_carrier_on(ameba_wifi_iface[STA_WLAN_INDEX]);
 
 	if (data->state == RTK_STA_CONNECTING) {
-- 
